1. Faye had 34 coloring books: \boxed{34}
2. She gave away 3 books: \boxed{-3}
3. The number of books she gave away is subtracted from the original number to find the number of books she had left after the giveaway: \boxed{34 - 3 = 31}
4. Then she bought 48 more books: \boxed{+48}
5. These purchases are added to the remaining books to find the net number of books Faye has: \boxed{31 + 48 = 79}

