 To solve this problem, let's first determine the total number of players.
To find the number of groups, we'll divide the total number of players by the number of players per group (6):
\begin{align*}
\text{{Total players }} &= \text{{Returning }} + \text{{New }} \\
                         &= 6 + 48 \\
                         &= 54
\end{align*}

\begin{align*}
\text{{Number of groups }} &= \frac{\text{{Total players}}}{\text{{Players per group}}} \\
                                &= \frac{54}{6}
\end{align*}

Now, we just need to simplify the fraction:
\begin{align*}
\text{{Number of groups }} &= 9
\end{align*}

So, there would be \boxed{9} groups with 6 players in each group.

