   - Hours worked on Monday: \boxed{8 hours}
   - Amount earned on Monday: \boxed{8\$/hour \times 8 hours = \boxed{64\$}}

2. Calculate the amount Will made on Tuesday:
   - Hourly wage: \boxed{8\$/hour}
   - Hours worked on Tuesday: \boxed{2 hours}
   - Amount earned on Tuesday: \boxed{8\$/hour \times 2 hours = \boxed{16\$}}

3. Sum the amounts earned on both days:
   - Total amount earned: \boxed{64\$ + 16\$ = \boxed{80\$}}

So, Will made \boxed{80\$} in those two days.

